WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:21.560
Ask the policy assistant a question about the fictional HR policies.

2
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:38.240
The question starts from an older leave rule.

3
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:44.720
The answer cites the current policy: five days, by 31 March.

4
00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:57.640
The answer draws on HR's policy library.

5
00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:03.640
The library keeps current and superseded policy versions labelled.

6
00:01:04.400 --> 00:02:22.640
Ask a visitor-policy question that the documents do not cover.

7
00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:29.760
The assistant records the general question for HR.

8
00:02:30.160 --> 00:03:05.320
Follow the question into its FlowOps workflow record.

9
00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:11.100
The HR queue keeps the general question and its reference.

10
00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:21.040
The recorded visitor question is waiting in the HR queue.

11
00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:25.080
An automated test records HR's answer and marks it approved.

12
00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:43.800
Board automation copies the approved answer to the assistant's answer board.

13
00:03:44.600 --> 00:04:36.600
Ask the same visitor question again.

14
00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:42.600
The recorded reply gives HR's approved answer with its reference.

15
00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:58.440
An automated test withdraws HR's answer.

16
00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:03.120
The record keeps the withdrawn text in its history.

17
00:05:03.840 --> 00:06:11.960
Ask the same question after the withdrawal.

18
00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:17.440
Follow the question through a fresh search and HR queue entry.
